  "content": {
    "text": "3 days ago\nFord and GM both got into the battery storage business, just in time for SpaceX's debut\nShares of Ford and GM outperformed the broader equity market on Friday -- and that could have something to do with SpaceX's trading debut.\nWall Street sees increased demand for stationary battery storage coming from SpaceX. And that's an area that both GM and Ford waded in deeper recently.\nAnalysts at Oppenheimer made that case this week, mostly connecting the dots to Tesla, of course. The EV maker's stationary storage business is \"a key beneficiary of [SpaceX’s] data center capacity spending,\" they said.",
